    "Create a premium 9:16 vertical editorial BACKGROUND ONLY for a Moneyberg U.S. stock market news graphic about the NASDAQ REBOUND after a sharp AI-stock selloff. Fresh cool cobalt blue, midnight navy and restrained teal palette, confident calm financial architecture. A modern stock-exchange atrium with dark smoked-glass surfaces, slim cobalt architectural light strips, brushed titanium columns and distant geometric exchange hall structure visible only in the bottom quarter. No people. No words, no digits, no prices, no chart, no graphs, no ticker symbols, no logos, no fake financial data. Do not create market screenshots.\nComposition at 1080x1920 equivalent: the main region x104\u2013961,y164\u20131536 will hold large accurately composed text and three data panels. Keep it quiet and dark navy, especially across the upper left and middle. Background imagery is most visible in the bottom quarter and along the outer right edge; understated visual depth, physical materials, no busy holograms. Later typography will use actual Lato Black weight900 for headline/labels/brand and actual Georgia for body/captions/sources. Exact brand later is MONEYBERG NEWS BRIEF, one compact secondary line at35px. Minimum authored text33px, body35px, headline51px. These are composition instructions; do not render text.\nReserve ONE empty circular antique-brass medallion recess in the far-right brushed-titanium structural column, approximately centered x985,y490, inner diameter144px at1080x1920 equivalent. This must be a front-facing flat circle, built into the architecture with subtle teal reflected light and believable contact shadows. Leave its interior completely blank, no portrait or inscription. The actual original Moneyberg gold coin PNG will be placed there later at exact circular proportions, entirely within the upper75% of the image (y<=1440), clear of content. Keep the full mounting ring visible. The final coin should belong to the architecture rather than float as a badge. Main market data overlays will begin below y708 so keep the mount above y670. Bottom view can show trading-hall infrastructure and reflective floor but no screens containing charts or writing. No watermark, no red box, no typography, no background-credit footer."
